From 3943e269e4df1477f4db9909e173e8f0f07b1248 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:20:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(providers): route configured providers by explicit prefix

Only `reliability.fallback_providers` were registered as ReliableProvider
extras, so a model reference such as `newapi/dpsk` for a provider that is
configured under `models.providers` but is not a fallback target was not
recognized: the prefix was stripped and the bare model was sent to the
primary provider, which rejected it ("Model dpsk is not allowed").
`/model newapi/dpsk` was therefore unusable.

Every configured provider is now also routable by an explicit
`provider/model` prefix. Routing and failover stay separate: the
`routable` entries are only consulted when the caller spells out the
provider prefix, while the failover chain still contains exactly the
`reliability.fallback_providers` (plus rotated keys) in their configured
order, so a bare model keeps its existing failover behavior.
